  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Thinly slice cucumber and red radish into rounds. Cut Japanese tofu into 1cm chunks.\n• In a small bowl, combine miso paste, sesame dressing and the honey. ~~~~~~~~~~ MODULAR STEP ~~~~~~~~~~"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook tofu, tossing until browned, 3-4 minutes.\n• Add miso glaze, tossing to coat, 1 minute. ~~~~~~~~~~ MODULAR STEP ~~~~~~~~~~ In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook tofu, tossing until browned, 3-4 minutes.\n• Add miso glaze, tossing to coat, 1 minute. TIP: Cook tofu in batches if your pan is getting crowded."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, in a large bowl, combine mayonnaise and Japanese style dressing.\n• Add shredded cabbage mix, mixed salad leaves, cucumber and radish. Toss to combine. Season with salt and pepper."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide slaw between bowls. Top with miso tofu bites. Spoon over any remaining glaze from pan.\n• Sprinkle over sesame seeds. Enjoy!"
    }
